                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "III. The Lord’s Final Judgment Chapter 3 The Day of the Lord - It shall come to pass I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh. Your sons and daughters will prophesy, your old men will dream dreams, your young men will see visions.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "2",
                       "number":  2,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Even upon your male and female servants, in those days, I will pour out my spirit.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "3",
                       "number":  3,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "I will set signs in the heavens and on the earth, blood, fire, and columns of smoke;",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "4",
                       "number":  4,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "The sun will darken, the moon turn blood-red, Before the day of the LORD arrives, that great and terrible day.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "5",
                       "number":  5,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Then everyone who calls upon the name of the LORD will escape harm. For on Mount Zion there will be a remnant, as the LORD has said, And in Jerusalem survivors whom the LORD will summon.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   }
               ],
